{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"mica-governing-buck","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\n`binding_store.py` is at the 800-line hard boundary because file loading, unknown-field preservation, tempfile cleanup, JSON encoding, GET-rotation ordering, retired-state replacement, and alert persistence live beside identity policy. Moving those branches without direct byte/fault oracles could turn known recoverable partial states into silent data loss.\n\n## Outcome\nExtract a private `BindingRepository`/unit-of-work behind the unchanged public `BindingStore` facade. The repository owns paths and the original dictionaries, returns open typed views over those same dictionaries, and preserves every existing load/save byte and exception contract. `peer_state.py` and `get_rotation.py` remain independent owners. Record the internal ownership and recovery/cutover constraints in the binding-lifecycle ADR.\n\n## Plan\n1. Add a cohesive repository module for live, retired, rotation, and alert paths; current load/corruption rules; JSON tempfiles; per-file `os.replace`; and dirty/change gating. Do not introduce a multi-file atomicity claim.\n2. Move persistence calls behind facade delegates without changing `BindingStore` construction, loader, public signatures, shared inner dictionaries, or caller-visible exceptions.\n3. Preserve rotation-before-live order and the inline rotation floor, retired-first move ordering, best-effort alert writes, and exact sorted/indented/newline serialization.\n4. Keep tickets publication in `reconcile_helpers.py` as an external five-file allowlisted seam. Add no broad staging and no publish at each local checkpoint.\n5. Add an ADR that distinguishes repository unit-of-work durability from tickets publication and records the later exact-match recovery boundary.\n\n## Testing (RED → GREEN)\n- A direct-repository suite loads legacy/unknown-field fixtures and asserts byte-equal round trips and no eager rewrite.\n- Failure cuts inject tempfile, rotation replace, retired replace, live replace, alert write, and selective commit failures. Oracles are exact surviving files/bytes, raised versus swallowed outcome, alert/tally, and unchanged HEAD where applicable.\n- Public-facade regressions assert pending/confirmed/reverse lookup and the current shallow `all_bindings()` compatibility.\n- Existing GET-rotation and selective-publication suites remain the cross-seam oracle.\n\n## Compatibility / rollback\nThis is an internal delegation only. Reverting the facade delegation restores the previous implementation over identical files. No format migration, eager rewrite, public import change, deep copy, general journal, or `git add -A` is permitted.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Given legacy records and unknown fields, direct repository and public-facade load/save preserve semantic fields and exact sorted/indented/trailing-newline bytes without an eager write.\n- [ ] Given each named fault cut, tests observe the documented old/new file combination and the same raise/swallow/alert behavior as before extraction.\n- [ ] GET rotation is durably attempted before live replacement; a failed sidecar save retains the newest inline floor and a later retry converges.\n- [ ] `BindingStore` import, constructor, loader, signatures, shared inner-entry behavior, and existing peer/get-rotation delegates remain compatible.\n- [ ] Tickets publication still stages only the existing five bridge-state files and an unchanged pass creates no commit.\n- [ ] The ADR states repository ownership, ordered partial-state behavior, selective publication, rollback, and the no-journal/no-format-migration decision.","id":"5142-4dbf-9469-4672","parent_id":"5e64-d9cd-2dd4-4036","priority":1,"tags":["rp02","reconciler","persistence","tdd"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"RP-02 S1 — Extract the byte-preserving binding repository"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787022424824041001,"uuid":"10f6e9e6-cf47-4914-8b11-b56d9010dc8a"}